screenshots/
*.png
*.jpeg
!docs/screenshots/*.png
# UI-Piktogramm-Masken: 19 Alphakanal-PNGs à ~3 KB, die die Kampfleiste als
# CSS-mask-image laedt. Sie muessen mit, sonst rendern die Ability-Knoepfe leer.
!frontend/public/ui-pictograms/*.png

# Dungeon enemy art: the generated raws stay local (42 files, ~141 MB — they would
# more than double the repo). Only the keyed AVIFs are tracked; those are what the
# ingest uploads to Supabase Storage anyway. Zuordnung Datei -> Gegner-id:
# docs/plans/dungeon-enemy-asset-manifest.md
assets/dungeon-enemies/raw/

# Temporary snapshot files
*-snapshot.md
*-snapshot.yml

# Database dumps
db-dump-*.sql

# One-off screenshot scripts
scripts/screenshot-*.mjs

# Playwright MCP browser automation logs
.playwright-mcp/

# Script-generated image gallery + A/B test outputs
# (populated by scripts/generate_ab_*_gallery.py, generate_real_instagram_gallery.py, etc.)
_test_output/

# DRIFT renderer dev harness (local preview only, not part of the Lit component)
frontend/drift-preview.html

# Prototyping spikes — vendored node_modules, never shipped
spikes/

# Claude Code session lock
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# UI pictograms: the magenta originals stay local (10 files, ~37 MB). The keyed
# masters in assets/ui-pictograms/ are the repo copy; regenerate them with
#   .venv/bin/python scripts/key_dungeon_enemy_art.py \
#       assets/ui-pictograms/raw assets/ui-pictograms --min-blob-share 0.02
# Provenance and acceptance measurements: docs/plans/ui-pictogram-prompts.md
assets/ui-pictograms/raw/
